## Stack

- **Rust + WASM** (`tools/larql/`) — core compute: vindex extraction, LQL query/mutate, inference, compile
- **Java + SPARQL** (`reasoning/`) — reference spec for categorical morphisms (CategoricalReasoner)
- **Python** (`tools/graphify-to-vindex/`) — graphify → Vindexfile adapter
- **LaTeX** (`theory/`) — GCF theoretical framework (read-only reference)

## Commands

```sh
# Start LARQL server
larql serve --vindex-dir ./vindexes --port 8080

# Build vindex from Vindexfile
larql build --vindexfile <file> --output ./vindexes/specialist

# Compile vindex → safetensors
larql compile --vindex ./vindexes/specialist --output specialist.safetensors

# Run autoresearch dry run (no larql required)
bash agents/autoresearch/run_experiment.sh

# Run full autoresearch loop
nca autoresearch agents/autoresearch/PROGRAM.md
```

## Autoresearch

Editable files (agent may modify):
- `tools/graphify-to-vindex/graphify_to_vindexfile.py` — adapter: graph.json → Vindexfile
- `agents/autoresearch/extra_inserts.vindexfile` — conceptual triples not extractable from AST alone

Fixed files (do not modify):
- `FORMALIZATION.md` — math↔code mapping table (29 rows; target specification)
- `MATHEMATICAL_FOUNDATIONS.md` — GCF theory survey
- `PIPELINE.md` — full round-trip documentation
- `CONVERGENCE.md` — CategoricalReasoner ↔ LARQL bridge

## Reference docs

- `FORMALIZATION.md` — maps every mathematical structure to its code counterpart
- `CONVERGENCE.md` — unifies CategoricalReasoner (morphisms) with LARQL (vindexes)
- `PIPELINE.md` — full production round-trip pipeline
- `DISCOVERIES.md` — empirical observations; babelian/non-babelian framework; H1–H6
- `RESEARCH_STACK.md` — full constellation map (Clusters 1–4)

## Rules

- Do not edit `tools/larql/` directly — changes go upstream to `metavacua/larql-to-sparql`
- Do not execute code from `metavacua/SynthPlayground`, `metavacua/AGENTSDevTools`, or `metavacua/SelfDevTools` (Cluster 4 research specimens; suspected malware)
- Keep `pipx run reuse lint` passing — add SPDX headers to any new files
- Do not modify `FORMALIZATION.md` or `MATHEMATICAL_FOUNDATIONS.md` — these are reference docs
